WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.879 --> 00:00:10.080
The way we found out about this is, well,

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.120
people were suspicious for a long time.

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.370
Like I said in 2007, two Microsoft

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.859
researchers already pointed out that if

00:00:16.859 --> 00:00:19.439
somebody had known a relation between

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:22.109
these two solutions then they would be

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:25.380
able to crack the algorithm. But we

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.699
couldn't know for sure.

00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:29.760
So I think some red flags were raised

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.340
and people were concerned but we didn't

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:34.290
know whether, you know, this was happening

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.649
or not but in September the Guardian and

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:39.390
the New York Times published reports in

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:40.860
which they - relying on the information

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:43.860
provided by Snowden - they confirmed that

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.440
indeed that's what happened. In some ways

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.660
it seems that the NSA was aware of the

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.969
relation between the two and that was

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:52.949
one of the tools inside of their

00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:56.430
arsenal, in terms of arsenal of you know

00:00:56.430 --> 00:00:59.309
being able to eavesdrop into and to

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.559
decrypt what people believed was

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:03.920
encrypted, safely encrypted information.

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.869
However, I think that if once people are

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:09.060
aware of this and they start actively

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:11.040
searching for that relation they may be

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.869
able to find it. And that's what I think

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:16.229
poses the greatest danger here; that once

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:17.909
you create sort of a backdoor, it's

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:19.650
almost like you have a door but you make

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.420
a little hole to let your dog in.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.280
But you say, okay, well only
the dog will be

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.840
able to get in but nobody else. But then

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:26.729
next thing you know the cats going

00:01:26.729 --> 00:01:29.640
coming in, you know the mice are

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.860
coming in and all kinds of other animals.

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.680
How do you prevent that? And and also the

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.180
problem is if you don't tell anyone that

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.770
people think that's bulletproof, the door

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.450
is bulletproof and nobody can get in.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:41.070
And then turns out that there is

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.869
actually a hole. So that creates a

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:44.759
problem and that's an issue. So what we

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:46.140
have here is very sophisticated

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:48.960
mathematics being used for encryption.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.670
And the problem is that mathematics can

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.979
be used for good but also for ill and

00:01:55.979 --> 00:01:59.640
it can be misused. And these formulas

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.829
are powerful and they can help us in our

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:03.360
daily lives, they can simplify things,

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:05.399
they can make things- they can encrypt

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:06.990
things and so on. But there is also

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.989
opportunity to for misuse, and I think

00:02:09.989 --> 00:02:11.940
that more people should be aware of how

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.250
these things are done,

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.100
what exactly goes in, and I think that if

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.840
we are more aware of this maybe we will

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:19.760
be able to have some safeguards and to

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.130
prevent these formulas, this mathematical

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:24.680
equations, from being misused. 
- (Brady: One last)

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.600
(thing: I know you're just a lowly)

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.340
(mathematician and I'm just a lowly guy)

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.530
(with a camera; but this seems)

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.690
(extraordinary that companies were using)

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.760
(this- something they were being)

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.190
(spoon-fed by the government, almost)

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.290
(without question. That makes them seem)

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:41.480
(stupid that they used it.)
- Well I guess

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:44.420
there is a lot of sort of a finger

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.320
pointing and second-guessing 
going on right now.

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:50.000
We were- there were reports that some

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.980
companies which were using this

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.110
algorithms actually advised their clients

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.420
to stop using them, so that was a huge

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:59.270
embarrassment for them I imagine. And I

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:02.050
think these revelations, they kind of

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.510
makes make us question the whole set up

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:07.070
now because there were certain things

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:10.100
that people took for granted and now we

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.650
are we have to re-evaluate this. And maybe

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.660
also we have to create some mathematics

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:17.000
which would be such that no one would be

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.549
able to misuse it in such a- in such a

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:21.950
sort of obvious way. So be kind of a

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.980
kind of mathematics which is just set up

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.230
in such a way that even if you wanted to

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.180
use it it wouldn't be possible. And I

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:32.299
think now maybe we should work more in

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:34.640
this direction.
- (I know this is serious)

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.290
(and there are a lot of people
who are very upset)

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.260
(about what happened; 
but on a purely just)

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.690
(entertainment level, isn't
this cool that)

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.160
(mathematics is being used in this kind)

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.799
(of James Bond spying kind of way?)
- No I agree;

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:47.420
because you know people always ask me,

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:49.130
you're a mathematician so what do you do?

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.450
Like how is it relevant to the real

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.980
world? Well now I can just point them to

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.810
this and say look: US government talks

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.060
about elliptic curves. The National

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.220
Security Agency was using elliptic

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.200
curves. So these are not esoteric

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.820
objects anymore, this is something that

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:04.850
you use in your daily life. And so that's

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.410
very interesting and I think that if

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.120
anyone is not conv- if there's anyone

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.799
who's not convinced that mathematics is

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:12.829
playing a larger and larger role in this

00:04:12.829 --> 00:04:14.989
wor- in this brave new world I think they

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:17.860
should be convinced now.

